  Quote of the Week:

  Desierius Erasmus, Dutch scholar, 1521:
  "Let a King recall that to improve his realm is better than to increase 
his territory."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  Winter melted into sweet spring.  Mugai's attempted cast of the Tornado 
spell didn't work.  A mysterious magical counterspell seemed to have worked 
against his spell.
  With the advent of the early summer season, Mugai travelled to Ngara.
  In late summer, Mugai rode into Chirfa.
  The hot days of summer surrendered to fall.  Mugai cast a Bless spell.  
The Amazonian Sea was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected 
no armies in the Amazonian Sea.
  During early winter, Mugai failed in his ineffectual attempt to cast a 
Tornado spell.  A mysterious magical counterspell seemed to have impeded his 
spell.


  A fleet sent by the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) 
entered the Barents Sea, hoping to subjugate that province owned by 
Cosmic Herderer Mugai and made up of great Seas.  The Barents Sea was 
overrun by Tao-Li (#32)'s fleet.  Tao-Li leads approximately 2 Bowmen, 1 
Axemen, 1 Whales, 2 Fleet and 1 Mermen.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Cosmic Herderer Mugai for this year.


  Mugai treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Mugai Treated with Hokuto, 
but Hokuto did not react favorably to his friendly overtures.  It is hoped 
that next year, both Kings will see the wisdom of Treating.
  Mugai treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Mugai treated with his ally 
II Kahn (#6).  Mugai treated with his ally Giovanna (#7).  Mugai treated 
with his ally Circe (#8).  Mugai treated with his ally Agesilao (#9).

  Here is the financial report for Mugai's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 13 gold in revenue.  2 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Mugai was left with 76 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Samantha
To: Mugai

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I cancelled my move to Tabora in order to fight for the 
province of Ngara.  Instead, I practiced my Exploring for months, but could 
make no significant progress.

  In Ngara, Cosmic Herderer Mugai brought to bay 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1).  I was in command of the invading 
armies.  The defending forces were commanded by the provincial garrison 
commander.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Ngara (0604):

