  DEFENDING ARMY

  I stood ready at the head of my thousands.  No generals were present to 
lead the forces of Uga-Buga Makumb.
  I was unlucky this time, because my rations were dwindling and my men had 
to fight on empty stomachs.  As the fierce battle intensified, the tactical 
wit of the acting commander and I appeared to be well matched.
  Mugai's soldiers swore to struggle desperately for their homeland.
  Across the whole front, the 213th Chariots faced the 6th Garrison.  The 
13th Garrison outflanked the enemy and charged in with full strength.  The 
213th Chariots fought the 6th Garrison and was almost powerless to stop 
their determined advance.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Mugai, a final 
determined thrust defeated their opponent and won the day for the acting 
commander.  The 6th Garrison destroyed the 213th Chariots.
  Samantha's armies were defeated and pushed out of Ngara.  My forces 
completely dispersed, I escaped frightened and alone to Chirfa.
  The wet spring blossomed into early summer.  I could not cast Plague on 
Jerbilia because I needed to be in or next to the target province.  Instead, 
I practiced my Necromancy and my skill in Necromancy went up.
  Midsummer's night passed and a hot late summer arrived.  I wasn't in 
Tabora so I utilized my fine covert skills to secretly keep track of 
happenings in Chirfa and reported the following information.  Chirfa owes 
allegiance to Cosmic Herderer Mugai.  Listening to the gossip of wanderers 
and mercenaries, one can deduce the rulership of surrounding provinces: 
Silvermist- Uga-Buga Makumb.
  Approximate Taxation: 2
  There were no conspicuous characters or forces in Chirfa.
  I also kept tabs on the characters in Chirfa and any further news is in 
the General Intelligence Report.

  With the advent of the fall season I could find no soldiers in Chirfa for 
the requested Legion troops.  Instead, I discovered nothing valuable in my 
sagely researches.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I attempted an illegal move.  
I tried to move from Chirfa to Jerbilia, a non-adjacent province.  Instead, 
I rode into Ngara.

  Thy humble servant,   Samantha


